    <span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Rentals</span>
    <h1>Hanoi Motorbike Rental: Long-stay Visitors Rental Paperwork Questions</h1>
    <p>A month-long rental is a contract with a month of consequences, and the paperwork conversation is where those consequences are decided while they are still cheap. The deposit's shape, the term's edges, the servicing arrangement, the licence and insurance questions: each is a five-minute question on day one or a week-long problem in week three. This page collects the questions a long-stay visitor should ask before signing, using verified business facts where they exist and cautious, shop-terms-only wording everywhere else, with nothing invented and no paraphrased law.</p>
    <p>The page belongs to the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> cluster and is written for long-stay visitors. The verified prices for every model and term sit on the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental-cost/">cost hub</a>, the general question bank is on the <a href="/faq/">FAQ</a> page, and the practical signing sequence is laid out in the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/how-to-rent-a-motorbike-in-hanoi/">how-to-rent guide</a>.</p>

    <nav class="toc" aria-label="Table of contents">
      <p>On this page</p>
      <ol>
        <li><a href="#sec-1">Why the long-stay contract deserves more questions</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-2">The term and the money questions</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-3">The deposit, asked properly</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-4">The licence and insurance questions</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-5">The servicing and mid-term questions</a></li>
